userContent.text:
Build an interactive figure using Chart.js.

CONCEPT: Titrating alanine with hydroxide converts it stepwise from a fully protonated cation through the neutral zwitterion to the carboxylate anion, with the pKa values at half-equivalence points and the isoelectric point at one full equivalent.
KEY INSIGHT (what students should walk away understanding): Each flat stretch of the curve is a 50:50 buffer where pH equals a pKa, and the isoelectric point sits midway between the two pKa values — the one pH where alanine exists almost entirely as the zero-net-charge zwitterion.
DEMO STEPS: 6 guided steps — implement the step player in #ui

